Hmmm. I think that might fix the NAMESPACE error. But not the postgresql errors.

Not sure how to fix the postgresql errors. These are the lines that cause the problems:

```
systemd.services.dex = {
    after = [ "networking.target" ] ++ (optional (cfg.settings.storage.type == "postgres") "postgresql.service");
    BindPaths = optional (cfg.settings.storage.type == "postgres") "/var/run/postgresql";
}
```

Maybe just make `systemd.services.dex.after` and `systemd.services.dex.BindPaths` configurable settings?

And add a `local_postgres` setting that sets the defaults?

Or maybe just add a check for `config.host == "/var/run/postgres"` - but this one seems a little bit yucky.
